      "message": "`set_bitstream_level_tier()` calls `aom_internal_error(\u0026ppi-\u003eerror, ...)` (`encoder.c:559`) if the new `(profile, level, tier)` combination is invalid. Because `av1_encode()` runs inside `av1_get_compressed_data()` where `cm-\u003eerror-\u003esetjmp \u003d\u003d 1`, jumping directly to `ppi-\u003eerror.jmp` skips resetting `cm-\u003eerror-\u003esetjmp \u003d 0` and leaves `cm-\u003eerror-\u003ejmp` pointing at a dead stack frame. Consider passing `struct aom_internal_error_info *error` to `set_bitstream_level_tier()` (`\u0026ppi-\u003eerror` in `init_seq_coding_tools()` and `cm-\u003eerror` here) so errors go through `av1_get_compressed_data()`\u0027s handler.",
